<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lady K'abel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lady K'abel was a princess of the Kaan dynasty of Calakmul who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-bahlam-ii">K'inich B'ahlam II</a>, king of Waka' (El Perú) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, in the 7th century. She held the title kaloomte', supreme warrior, ranking above her husband, and sealed the alliance between the two cities. Her tomb was discovered at El Perú in 2012.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lady-kabel.jpg" alt="Lady K'abel" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clevelandart_1967.29.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
